## What a smart city is

Smart cities are large developments built around the idea of living, working and relaxing in one place: homes, offices, schools, shops, sports and green spaces in a single master plan. Each one holds a certificate from the Economic Development Board.

## What foreigners can buy

A townhouse, villa, apartment, penthouse or duplex in any approved smart city. A purchase of **USD 375,000 or more** comes with a residence permit.

According to the EDB, holders of a residence, occupation or permanent residence permit could also buy a serviced plot of up to 2,100 m² to build on, but only if the purchase was made no later than 30 June 2022.

## The two smart cities on the west coast

The EDB's 2025 summary of smart city projects lists sixteen certificate holders. Two are on our coast:

- **Cap Tamarin**, located in [Tamarin](/en/areas/tamarin), planned with residential, commercial, education and leisure zones and a park with a green belt.
- **Medine Smart City** (Uniciti), which the EDB lists under [Flic en Flac](/en/areas/flic-en-flac), with an education village including universities and private schools, residential estates, a business park, a medical facility, a sports complex and an arts centre.

Ask each developer which phases are for sale and whether a given home qualifies for a residence permit.

## Costs and process

The buying steps are explained in [how buying works](/en/living-in-the-west/how-buying-works). Ask your notary for the registration duty that applies to your purchase.

*Rules and amounts change. Everything here was checked against the Economic Development Board's own pages on 2 October 2026; confirm the details with the EDB, your notary and the developer before you sign.*
